<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Republic of Texas</h1><p class="st-meta">1836 CE – 1845 CE · capital Austin</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Lone Star Republic, which broke away from Mexico in 1836 and stayed independent for nearly ten years before joining the United States.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>From the 1820s <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mexico">Mexico</a> invited American settlers, led by empresarios such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stephen-f-austin">Stephen F. Austin</a>, into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coahuila">Coahuila</a> y <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hasinai-confederacy">Tejas</a>. Tension over centralist rule and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> led to revolt in 1835. Independence was declared at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/washington-on-the-brazos">Washington-on-the-Brazos</a> on 2 March 1836; after the fall of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alamo-mission">Alamo</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sam-houston">Sam Houston</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-lopez-de-santa-anna">Santa Anna</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-san-jacinto">San Jacinto</a> in April.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The republic had a president, congress and constitution modelled on the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a>, and it protected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">Cotton</a> farming expanded and settlers poured in with offers of free land. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mexico">Mexico</a> never recognised independence and raided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-antonio">San Antonio</a> in 1842. Debts mounted, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mirabeau-b-lamar">Mirabeau Lamar</a>'s ill-fated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texan-santa-fe-expedition">Santa Fe Expedition</a> failed, and policy towards the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/comanche">Comanche</a> swung between war and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sam-houston">Houston</a>'s attempts at peace. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austin-texas">Austin</a> became the capital in 1839.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Most Texans wanted annexation, delayed in Washington by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> question. Congress approved it in 1845, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a> became the 28th state in December. The annexation was a cause of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexican-american-war">Mexican-American War</a> of 1846 to 1848.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/republic-of-texas.jpg" alt="Republic of Texas" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Pumbaa80. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Republic_of_Texas_(1836%E2%80%931839).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1836 CE – 1845 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Austin</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Sam Houston, Mirabeau B. Lamar, Anson Jones</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Protestantism, Roman Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English, Spanish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-states">United States</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Texas Republic, Lone Star Republic</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1840&amp;focus=republic-of-texas" aria-label="Republic of Texas on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2144 1072 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Republic of Texas lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M2464 1328L2321 1717M2464 1328L2570 1008"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M2321 1717h0M2570 1008h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2464 1328h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M2464 1328h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Austin. <a href="/atlas?year=1840&amp;focus=republic-of-texas">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
